# =====================================================================================
# GWIscan family table — MULTI-FAMILY mode (families grouped under a multi-family)    
# =====================================================================================
# Copy this file to  config/multi-family.tsv  and edit it for your study families,
# and set  MODE: multi-family  in config.yaml.
#
# Multi-family mode adds a multi-family rollup on top of the per-family results
# (for example Lectin over GNA, Legume, CRA). Every processing step matches family
# mode; the leading Multifamily column drives the rollup.
#
# One row per family. TAB-separated. Whole-line '#' comments and blank lines are
# ignored (put each comment on its own line beginning with '#').
#
# COLUMNS  (family-mode columns, with a leading Multifamily column)
#   Multifamily   The grouping label this family rolls up into. Required in this
#                 mode; families sharing a value are reported together.
#
#   Family        Study family name. Used verbatim in outputs and domain ids
#                 (GNA gives AthGNA001.1). Required and unique.
#
#   PfamModel     How the family is IDENTIFIED — one of:
#                   PFxxxxx   Pfam accession: hmmsearch + DIAMOND.
#                   name.hmm  custom family-specific HMM in db/hmm/ (NAME line must
#                             equal the Family): hmmsearch + DIAMOND. Use when the
#                             family's Pfam is a shared or ancestral domain.
#                   -         no HMM: DIAMOND only.
#
#   BlastModel    Reference protein FASTA (in db/blast/) used as the DIAMOND round-1
#                 query. DIAMOND runs for every family, so this is required for all.
#
#   InterProModel Optional. Accession(s) that CONFIRM a candidate via InterProScan; a
#                 candidate is kept when it carries any of them. One of three, by
#                 prefix: PF... (Pfam), cd... (CDD), PTHR... (PANTHER). Pipe-separated
#                 for alternatives. GWIscan enables the matching applications
#                 automatically. Blank falls back to the PfamModel accession. A family
#                 with no usable Pfam model (PfamModel = -) can still be confirmed by
#                 giving a CDD or PANTHER accession here; a family with neither is not
#                 confirmed.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Multifamily	Family	PfamModel	BlastModel	InterProModel
# specific Pfam -> hmmsearch + DIAMOND, confirmed on that Pfam:
Lectin	GNA	PF01453	AAA33346.1.fasta
Lectin	Legume	PF00139	AAA33983.1.fasta
# Lacks Pfam so confirmed using PANTHER accession:
Lectin	EUL	-	ABW73993.1.fasta	PTHR31257
